                <pb facs="0030" n="12" sameAs="frus:frus1948v03/pg12"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On January 22, 1948, Ernest Bevin delivered a speech in the British House of
                    Commons suggesting the “consolidation of Western Europe.” He mentioned the
                    Anglo-French Treaty of Dunkirk as a basis of cooperation and indicated that
                    similar agreements would be proposed to the Benelux countries.</p>
                <p>For text, see <hi rendition="#italic">Parliamentary Debates</hi>, House of
                    Commons, 1947–48, 5th series, volume 446, columns 383 ff.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
